\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Wing motion through the two halves of the flapping cycle, for the sinusoidal pitch kinematics with $\delta _0 \in \{0, \frac  {\pi }{2}, -\frac  {\pi }{2}, \pi \}$ and for the constant pitch simplification. Across all panels, $\psi _0 = 0$ and $\psi _1 = 45^\circ $. The top row shows the first half-stroke (wing moving along $-\hat  {s}$, with $\hat  {s}$ pointing right) and the bottom row the second half-stroke, along $+\hat  {s}$. Arrows indicate the direction of motion, the hollow circle marks the wing leading edge, and snapshots are taken at equal time increments, crowding near the stroke reversals where the flapping motion slows. The constant pitch kinematics match the $\delta _0 = \pi /2$ kinematics well, except near stroke reversal.}}{6}{figure.caption.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:pitch-kinematics}{{3}{6}{Wing motion through the two halves of the flapping cycle, for the sinusoidal pitch kinematics with $\delta _0 \in \{0, \frac {\pi }{2}, -\frac {\pi }{2}, \pi \}$ and for the constant pitch simplification. Across all panels, $\psi _0 = 0$ and $\psi _1 = 45^\circ $. The top row shows the first half-stroke (wing moving along $-\hat {s}$, with $\hat {s}$ pointing right) and the bottom row the second half-stroke, along $+\hat {s}$. Arrows indicate the direction of motion, the hollow circle marks the wing leading edge, and snapshots are taken at equal time increments, crowding near the stroke reversals where the flapping motion slows. The constant pitch kinematics match the $\delta _0 = \pi /2$ kinematics well, except near stroke reversal}{figure.caption.4}{}}
